      "comment": "What an item is about, in the words the owner's own content keeps using: a word is a topic once the titles of at least `least` items use it (a subject, an event's summary, a note) and no more than `share` percent of them do, so the owner's content extends the reader as it arrives. A word the kind reader already reads as a cue, a person's name, or a quiet word is never a topic. An item is about the topics its title and words use, at most `most`. The lexicon is learned in the browser and never leaves it.",
